<h1>The logic, drawn</h1>
<p class="lede">If a coupling can't be drawn, we probably don't understand it yet. Nine figures — eight authored in Mermaid, one a hand-authored SVG — each restating part of the argument in a second notation, and each a claim that can be wrong. Download any of them as SVG (vector) or PNG.</p>

<div class="figures">
{% for f in figures %}
  <figure class="fig" id="fig-{{ f.n }}">
    <div class="fig-head">
      <span class="fig-num">Fig. {{ f.n }}</span>
      <h2>{{ f.title }}</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="fig-assert">{{ f.asserts | safe }}</p>
    <div class="fig-canvas">
      {% if f.svg %}
      <div class="fig-art" data-fig="{{ f.n }}" data-kind="svg">{{ f.svg | safe }}</div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="fig-art" data-fig="{{ f.n }}" data-kind="mermaid"><div class="fig-loading">rendering figure {{ f.n }}…</div><pre class="fig-src" hidden>{{ f.code }}</pre></div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="fig-tools">
      <button type="button" class="fig-btn" data-dl="svg" data-fig="{{ f.n }}">↓ SVG</button>
      <button type="button" class="fig-btn" data-dl="png" data-fig="{{ f.n }}">↓ PNG</button>
    </div>
  </figure>
{% endfor %}
</div>

<p class="fig-foot">
  Source of truth: <a href="{{ '/docs/diagrams/' | url }}">docs/DIAGRAMS.md</a> (also renders on GitHub).
  Open the <a href="{{ '/viz/diagrams.html' | url }}">standalone figures</a> or the
  <a href="{{ '/viz/systems-theory-map.html' | url }}">landscape &amp; panel map</a>.
  Contested claims point to the <a href="{{ '/logs/open_questions/' | url }}">open questions</a>.
</p>

